ingredients:
  - "3/4 cup wheat flour"
  - "1 1/2 cup grated radish"
  - "1 tbsp oil/ghee"
  - "2 green chillies, chopped"
  - "1/2 tsp ginger paste"
  - "A few coriander leaves, chopped"
  - "1/4 tsp turmeric powder"
  - "1/2 tsp carom seeds"
  - "1/2 tsp sesame seeds"
  - "Water (as required)"
  - "Salt to taste"
instructions:
  - "Knead wheat flour into a smooth dough and keep aside for half an hour."
  - "Chop green chillies and coriander leaves."
  - "For the filling, heat 1 tsp oil, sauté grated radish, mix chopped chillies, coriander leaves, ginger paste, turmeric powder, and salt into the grated radish."
  - "Divide the dough and filling into four portions."
  - "Roll out each dough portion into a small roti, place one portion of stuffing in the center, bring the edges together, and press firmly."
  - "Roll the stuffed dough into a paratha and shallow fry, smearing oil."
  - "Let both sides of the paratha turn golden brown."
  - "Serve hot with curd or pickle."
